r or artifact repo declares facts in [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]its ref spec and inherits querying, relations, grouping, marks, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]copy, help and chrome without shipping code, so a new sub-tab [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]feature is implemented once and appears in every configured [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]provider's tab — including providers belonging to users we will [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]never see.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]10[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]artifacts_pane_contract.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/artifacts_pane_contract.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-m6[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-m6/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Live defects, golden fixtures, and the conformance harness[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]foundation[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]foundation: make provider tabs deterministic and failure-visible, then [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]freeze golden query/relation/persistence fixtures from current Patch [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]behavior and stand up the conformance harness every later phase extends.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Detail bands render the provider's declared fields[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #5FD7AF] xsmall [/bold black on #5FD7AF]\n    [#AF87FF]detail[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]detail: parameterize ordered_plan_property_items by the provider's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]declared ref.detail.fields so a document tab shows its own properties [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]instead of plan properties.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One typed entry target on every pane[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]identity[dim] · [dim][/dim]after foundation[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]identity: promote ArtifactEntryTarget to a typed value carrying pane [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]identity with a canonical token round-trip, give Patch a row target and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a real navigator, make ArtifactEntryNavigator an ABC, and retire [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]index-based marks and jump anchors.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]ArtifactsPaneContract and derived, explainable capabilities[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]after identity, detail[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]contract: introduce ArtifactsPaneContract with a closed PaneCapability [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]vocabulary derived from declared data by named auditable rules, collapse[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]every ref-prefix dispatch site onto it, and add the synthetic [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]third-party provider fixture.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The shared shell and its visual grammar[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]shell[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]shell: build the one chrome every pane renders through, specify and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]implement the five canonical pane states, and replace drifting provider [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]accents with a deterministic perceptual palette.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One query engine across every pane and both evaluators[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold white on #AF5FFF] xlarge [/bold white on #AF5FFF]\n    [#AF87FF]query[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]query: replace three query dialects with one profile-parameterized [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]engine spanning the Rust parser, the Rust batch corpus and the Python [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reference evaluator, move Patch to the inline filter bar, and namespace [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]slots, history and selection memory per pane.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Relations, reveal, and grouping as contract features[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]relations[dim] · [dim][/dim]after query, shell[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]relations: generalize the ancestors/children/siblings jumpers into [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]declared hierarchy, family and link relations rendered by a host-owned [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel, make reveal a reversible lens, and put every pane's grouping on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the shared fold registry.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The declarative ref.pane block[/bold #D7AFFF]                                [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]declare[dim] · [dim][/dim]after relations[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]declare: add the Python-side ref.pane block and its presentation digest [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]so a sidecar declares row template, sort, facets, grouping and empty [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]state as data, and ship it in the research provider.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Unified Artifacts keymap with a safe migration[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]keymap[dim] · [dim][/dim]after relations[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]keymap: unify the six Artifacts verbs whose meanings are inverted [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]between Patch and its siblings, shipped together with action aliases, a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]doctor advisory and a one-shot config migration.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Conformance, diagnostics, docs, and the performance gate[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]conform[dim] · [dim][/dim]after declare, keymap[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]conform: close the epic with a parametrized conformance suite over every[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]resolved sub-tab including a synthetic provider, ACE-surfaced provider [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]diagnostics, the documented contract, and the navigation performance [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-m6","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-m6.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-d6e3c29c1bcb14c2aea26b854ec257d1","started_at":"2026-08-14T21:08:56.254835+00:00","state":"active"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"8da32a0bb6b5750269598c462cc6a876de55fcbb99c4bb3bc9f171f63cd21120","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-m6.9/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"23245f6ae8eb998bda29c04da084d31794884f289af7f60dd53aa1738631e08b","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-m6.9/meta.json","size_bytes":633},"prompt":{"digest":"a897d4de93e3a782163345b0f90c6ab47a769cb85ff7757d3d841b3fd18bc3eb","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-m6.9/prompt.md","size_bytes":148},"state":{"digest":"2af7baa2b751039bb412b2c0f2bf2293539a1b963bf9ee65a3ae15f3cc74b1bb","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-m6.9/state.json","size_bytes":163}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-m6.9","local_name":"sase-